WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:16.480
This is the early 90s.
This is the time that the Soviet bloc

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:29.600
had just broken,
and a lot of these former Soviet countries

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.800
gained their independence,
and we had a lot of new collectives:

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:44.240
Hungary, Romania, all these countries,
Poland. So, as these collectives

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.680
would come to Cabella for the pujas,
Shri Mataji would invite them

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:54.160
to come on stage and sing something.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:02.720
So, this was Navratri Puja
and the Romanian collective was singing.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.920
And this was the first time
that they were on the stage.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:10.240
And they were trying
to sing Marathi songs.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.360
So, obviously,
their pronunciation was off.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:24.600
And we were about three, four yogis
from India, and we found them

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.960
so much out of tune.
So, when there was an interval, we left.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:36.520
So, the next morning,
Shri Mataji called us and asked,

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.760
"Why did you leave?"
So, we said, "You know,

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.000
they were totally off."&nbsp;

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.760
So, she said, "I was sitting there

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:57.200
and I was bestowing siddhis on them.
I was giving them vibrations

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:03.880
so that they will become great musicians.
And you should have been there

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.600
to stand by me."
So, we pulled our ears

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.200
and begged her forgiveness.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.240
I had a question.
So, I asked Shri Mataji

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:23.720
that how come those people
who don't have any natural talent

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:30.520
for singing, how can they come up
in [Quebec] in comparison

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.160
to people who are gifted,
who are born with a gift?

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:43.560
So, she said, "It doesn't matter to me
whether they are gifted or not gifted.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:52.680
When I bestow a siddhi on somebody,
it's like a seed that I plant.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:59.200
As you understand, a seed
has got all microscopic seeds in it.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.400
It has the power to manifest
all the powers of a tree.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.840
In the same way,
human beings were created.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:18.440
And as the seed is again recreated&nbsp;

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.560
in the flower or in the fruit,

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:35.000
it manifests itself in the same manner
as the basic tree had done.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.000
In the same way, you can say
that every human being

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:47.760
also has all these seeds in it.
And then that seed sprouts.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:56.040
As long as they keep doing Sahaja Yoga,
they keep me in their heart,

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.000
one day this will become
a very big tree."

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:06.720
So, sure enough,
next time when we came,

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:14.320
these very Romanians were singing
Qawwalis in Urdu

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:20.800
with such perfect accent,
with total tuning,

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:25.280
that even Nusrat Fateh Ali Khan
would be surprised.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:54.800
Another time, she was teaching
French yogis Marathi songs.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:55.880
This was in Paris.&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.920
And they were just not getting it.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:13.520
You know, the French Vishuddhi
and Marathi Vishuddhi are poles apart.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:25.240
So, after a lot of patience
that she had, they finally got it.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.120
And that year, we had
the Maharashtra tour,

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:51.160
which was a one-month tour
throughout all the villages.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:59.840
And in each, before every program,
these musicians were asked to sing.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.760
And these French yogis
sang these Marathi songs.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.880
And the audience
was absolutely impressed.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:13.640
And they couldn't imagine
that these French yogis are singing

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:19.360
so beautifully Marathi songs.
So, they were our advertisement

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.280
for Sahaja Yoga.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:28.080
So, one of the things
that she mentioned then, that yes,

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:39.640
"I give you these powers,
I give you all these talents, siddhis,

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:46.240
but you have to share with others.
Otherwise, you will get an ego

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:51.320
that I have become such a big musician.
And then that ego will come in the way.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.000
And then your music
will start going down."

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.040
So, the nectar should end in sharing.
How much we share?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:07.520
How much can we share?
When it comes to the nectar

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.520
of God's love,
how can we alone have it?

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.720
Cannot enjoy.
There's no enjoyment at all.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:23.240
The people who are going to enjoy
the nectar should have competition

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:26.480
in sharing that nectar
by which they get more and more of that.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.440
Who shares more?
Who is more generous?

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:39.080
So, you have to share.
If you've got the siddhi of a musician,

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:42.360
then you must teach it
to new young people.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:47.240
And have patience,
the same patience that she had with you.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:51.120
If you're a writer,
then you should have the patience

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:56.680
to teach other young people.
Whatever craft, whatever things

00:07:56.680 --> 00:08:01.000
that you have been blessed with,
will be shared.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.400
And with lot of love
and lot of patience.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:11.560
Only those who are meek in heart
will inherit the blessings of Mother.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.920
And you'll be surprised
how it will spread.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.080
All these musicians
who've come up in Sahaja Yoga,

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.640
all these talented people,
they didn't even know the language,

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:29.200
they didn't even know ABC,
they didn't even know the source.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:37.840
But through this gift that she bestowed,
they became much greater.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:44.520
They even, with their hard work,
with their dedication,

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:48.880
they even became better
than those who were born with the gift.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.600
Because those who are born with the gift
think, "Oh, you know, I'm born with it,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:58.120
so nobody can take it away from me
and it'll stay with me."

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:08.960
But they don't achieve perfection.
She said you have to attain excellence.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:14.320
Mediocrity has no place in Sahaja Yoga.
Only through excellence you'll enjoy.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:20.400
Only through excellence
you will really become Sahaja Yogis.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:28.080
But these who were not gifted
and they were blessed,

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.560
much further than these people.
So it doesn't matter

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:42.840
if you didn't have the opportunity
in your childhood for whatever reasons,

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:47.320
but you had interest in these things.
After you come to Sahaja Yoga,

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:51.880
with her blessings,
you can attain all these things.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:56.880
And those who have attained it
have to be collective.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:03.200
"I've been called today,
so you come and sit with me.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:08.080
And then you also sing."
So then they'll get confidence.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:13.240
It is how to inspire
confidence in others.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:21.160
I remember there was a novice
who had never been on the mic,

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.800
who had never spoken on the mic,
and she said,

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.800
"Okay, you anchor this show."
And the guy was so nervous.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:31.440
And he kept looking at her,
smiling and nodding at him.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:36.760
And after that, a few years later,
he was anchoring all the programs

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:45.880
in Ganpatipule. So she blesses you.
She opens that chakra.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:51.520
And then it takes over.
So we don't claim

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:59.440
that this is my talent
or this is my siddhi.

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:03.360
It's her blessings.
Whatever is, is coming from her.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:06.880
And that will take it forward.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:13.160
Then she recited one verse,
which she said,

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:24.160
there is no plant in nature
which doesn't have a medicinal quality.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:35.720
God has created nothing
which doesn't have some purpose,

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:50.520
some virtue. But you have to have
the discretion to take it out.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.880
Discretion to see it,
to see the potential of others

00:11:54.960 --> 00:12:01.680
and help them.
Not thinking of himself,

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.520
he's thinking of others.
How to bring them up?

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:13.520
By patience, by love, by sharing.
That is Sahaja Yoga.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:19.840
If somebody's called on the stage
to offer flowers,

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:23.000
and somebody else hasn't,
you should ask, "Okay, you come along.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:26.680
You offer flowers.
I have already done it.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:35.920
I've been called forward,"
or that we'll get some special blessing,

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:40.440
we are garlanding.
You're only the instrument,

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:46.880
only the hand of the collective.
And the more you realize that,

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:53.320
the more collective you become.
So even if you've done something,

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.000
give credit to the others.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:13:05.520
There was dinner
and the hostess had made pasta

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:09.120
and Shri Mataji enjoyed it
and she said, "Who has made it?"

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:13.000
And she gave, said, "All these ladies
who are helping, they have made it."

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:18.200
So she gave them the credit.
Not that Shri Mataji doesn't know

00:13:18.200 --> 00:13:22.000
who has made it. She is antaryami.
She knows everything.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:27.560
But she's pleased that you are
giving credit to others.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:34.520
And she's displeased when people
always claim credit for everything:

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:42.680
"I've done this. I've done that. I did."
That doesn't please her at all.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:49.640
Same way, if somebody has done something
and everybody's praising you,

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:53.680
try to share that credit
or give credit to the others.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:59.040
That is a way
that they will be encouraged.

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:07.600
So, this is how to please the Goddess.
Thank you.

